{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/612008-new-ideas-to-counter-well-informed-players","id":612008,"title":"New ideas to counter well informed players","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-02T03:17:34-07:00","id":612008,"title":"New ideas to counter well informed players","content":"One of my biggest issues with running games anymore is the fact my players are jaded and blase about what they encounter. If I desccribe a man who pulses and shifts into a gigantic man-bear they automatically know that its a Gurahl or if I'm being mean an elder gangrel.<br /> <br /> To counter this in my newest game (using nWoD rules and pick and choosing from conversion books), I am 1 making them start as mortals and not informing them which game line(s) I intend to use.<br /> <br /> I however would also like to give them new threats/beings out there to deal with.<br /> <br /> My first thought is a couple hundred years ago an archmage obsessed with werewolves and the fera got it into his head to start experimenting to create his own Garou, Bastet etc. Of course such a thing is virtually impossible and so he was only able to create individuals who could physically transform but had none or only partial access to the spiritual gifts of the fera (stepping sideways, gnosis, gifts etc). What he did not expect (or maybe he did he was crazy after all) was that those he gifted with such power would pass it down along their own bloodlines. However over the years lore was lost and not every child was gifted so the rites and rituals needed to awaken their powers were lost.<br /> <br /> The PCs of course would end up in a situation where they are forced to attempt to stop or inadvertantly reawaken several of these quasi-shifters.<br /> Thoughts? Suggestions on this idea?<br /> <br /> Thoughts on other new threats to lace into the World of Darkness? Id like things that bend but do not necessarily break or violate the various themes.<br /> My idea playing playing to Mage's ideas of consensual reality- the mages pattern tampering of these families so closely resembles the fera who are deeply seeded in humanities primal unconscious minds that paradox doesn't affect them in quite the same ways it would a true mage casting, however it would force certain issues- reduced regeneration, limited time in crinos, etc.<br /> For werewolf it is well known that mages stole the power of naming and routinely violate gaias balance and the weavers works with their art. This would be but one example of their blasphemy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/494-exalted-viovode","name":"Exalted Viovode","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T07:21:40-07:00","id":612210,"title":"","content":"Since you're already using nWoD rules, go for nWoD books on the &quot;blue line&quot;. Changing Breeds, Skinchangers, Inferno, Immortals, Antagonists, all that.<br /> <br /> Mystery and high variability are both pillars of the nWoD, so those books already have a LOT of material for you to work, even if your players read them themselfs.<br /> <br /> Skinchangers in particular will help you a lot with the idea of the artificial CBs, whyle nWoD Changing Breeds can work for the more developed ones and yet surprise your PCs a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T19:23:15-07:00","id":614405,"title":"","content":"I routinely take an interesting creature from the Cthulhu Mythos, rub off the serial #, adapt it to the WoD backstory, and be sure to describe it - never call it by whatever name it is known in stories or by Chaosium. If you are looking for a strange Wyrm creature to use against werewolves, it works wonderfully. Good for Mages too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T19:38:52-07:00","id":614417,"title":"","content":"Don't stop with Lovecraft, a lot of contemporary horror can be mined for &quot;surprises&quot;. In my own Chronicles I have used Stephen King: It, The Shining, and while I haven't used Christine I have ideas for it. I have also used Robert R McCammon: Bethany's Sin, Baal, and Night Boat. I did not use Wraith when adapting the Overlook not psychic powers. My players literally cringe and begin whimpering when they hear the word Derry. If your players are jaded then change that man who just changed into a bear be a Animage who to work spheres magic must be in bear form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T00:09:29-07:00","id":614677,"title":"","content":"A question occurred to me about my idea of artificial shifters- Due to their lack of shifter souls (the merged avatar)- would they still be capable of awakening?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/494-exalted-viovode","name":"Exalted Viovode","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T00:10:36-07:00","id":614688,"title":"","content":"I like the Cthulhu mythos ideas, also was considering fantastic pocket realms in the umbra","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/494-exalted-viovode","name":"Exalted Viovode","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T07:20:53-07:00","id":615040,"title":"","content":"Have you tried changing genre or story approach? You didn't specify what tends to happen when your players meet the bear-dude. But if usually it's a fight scene, maybe the bear-dude can be searching for help, or a red herring, or bait in a trap. If the bear-dudes are usually friendly, maybe it does attack, and the players have to figure out why.<br /> <br /> If you always use Gurahl in a particular way (I admit, I don't know very much about them), then maybe if you have the next one behaving against type, then you can catch your players' interest that way. Use their expectations against them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T15:07:36-07:00","id":615620,"title":"","content":"Its actually possible that both Mokole and Gurahl could be more accurately represented in nWoD as far as their power since nWoD doesn't allow for multiple actions the way cWoD does.<br /> <br /> As far as behavior- Gurahl are not likely to ask Garou for help, partly because they can generally handle their own business, partly because they have their own ways to call other Gurahl for aid, and mostly because of the fact Garou are more likely to kill a Gurahl then help it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/494-exalted-viovode","name":"Exalted Viovode","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"123"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T18:59:03-07:00","id":615896,"title":"","content":"That's kind of what I mean. I'd imagine your players know as much about Gurahl as you do, or could find out if they wanted to. So if the next time you use a Gurahl, it actually does ask them for help, they'll realize that there must be something fairly big or wrong happening, and hopefully decide that it warrants further investigation. (Granted, they may start wondering about it after killing the Gurahl, but that's Garou for you. :-))","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2430-kalinara","name":"kalinara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2430_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"582"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T00:51:40-07:00","id":616070,"title":"","content":"Maybe you should talk with your players. They are being assholes about this. Just because I know most WW material by heart doesn't mean I won't enjoy a game and that I cannot differentiate between what I know an what my characters know. They need to be in wonder to even see rare things popping up, and getting to interact with them, as for their characters these are singular occurrences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T01:23:18-07:00","id":616083,"title":"","content":"I'd recommend going through things as regular, baseline humans for a while at first. Like a game of Call of Cthulhu, begin them as a group of investigators, slowly drawn into the world of the supernatural. Make them FEEL the fear of being confronted with monsters and dangers beyond mortal ken, without any of the supernatural advantages they normally enjoy. Describe the ferocious beasts in deep, descriptive detail, while refusing to give overt hints as to what they are. Push the bloody horror of a vampire supping the juices from a victim behind the alley in the players faces. Have a deranged looking person screw with a PC's mind, and let them wonder if its a vampire or Mage or unAwakened Psychic or Changeling, or something even weirder. Have their be...<i>things</i> just beyond sight that defy description.<br /> <br /> Make them fully aware of just how frighteningly ignorant they are. Challenge them on what they think they know, and don't be afraid to bend the rules, or present unorthodox &quot;builds&quot; of normally iconic splats. Is that a Malkavian with Protean? An old clan Tzimisce with Obfuscate? A Setite with Dominate? Is it a Marauder? Or maybe its a crazed hedge wizard with potent shapeshifting, mind control, and Psychic Invisibility? Or maybe it's a Wraith (or Specter, or Risen), or some kind of Umbrood, or a Fomori? Your players don't know, and you shouldn't give the answer readily.<br /> <br /> Maybe the group investigates a weird cult. But are they Acolytes armed with Charms and Talismans? Or do they all have Sorcery (there is a difference, but it can be hard to tell if you do it right)? And what are they trying to summon? A demon? A powerful bane spirit? Something from beyond the furthest ring? Might they be summoning something physical, and merely moving a threat to them? They might not summon anything at all, and just be a bunch of occultists barking up the wrong tree.<br /> <br /> After a while, when the players have started becoming used to the idea that you aren't going to make them all into vampires or whatever, start laying out opportunities to advance into the supernatural. Have them pick up journals filled with knowledge, allowing them to start learning hedge magic. Or make one of them start getting headaches, and hear voices, until they start developing Psychic powers of their own. Or plant clues that one character might be related to the Garou.<br /> <br /> Perhaps, in their desire to learn more magic, the budding sorcerer starts looking for teachers. And one offers them power - only for them to turn out to be a Tremere, looking to Embrace. Alternatively, the party makes an enemy of a vampire, but the Lick decides the only fitting revenge would be to curse them with undeath. So one of the characters wakes up in a ditch at night, with a grisly thirst and no idea who embraced him or what kind of vampire he is.<br /> <br /> Or if you want to drop magic on players out of nowhere, give them a book with occult knowledge in it. And when they finish reading it, surprise them by saying &quot;Congratulations, your mind was completely blown by the revelations in this book! You no longer see the world the same way as before! Mark yourself as gaining one Arete!&quot; Turns out the otherwise innocuous occult book was a Primer the whole time. And now the entire party (or whichever ones haven't become vampires or had their First Change) has the option of reading this book and becoming Mages. But do they do it? Cosmic power seems like a sweet deal, but if any of them do have Path magic, they might have reservations about suddenly making an enemy of reality in the form of Paradox.<br /> <br /> And if somehow the entire party dies, that's okay! You can either have a passing group of vampires (or the vampire enemies they were fighting) embrace them on a lark, or have them all manifest in the Shadowlands as Wraiths!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-08T09:28:58-07:00","id":620172,"title":"","content":"One time I had a I-know-all player that subtitled all I storytelled to other players &quot;Oh, sure, that's a Brujah.. probably the rogue childe of the Brujah Elder&quot; , &quot;Oh, surely a Tzimisce wardog&quot; , &quot;That should be a Corax&quot;.<br /> One time, while scavenging a graveyard, they exhumed a torpid Highlander (from the Immortal: The Gathering fan-gameline). The Immortal thanks and goes his way.<br /> Other than an interesting storyline, I couldn't resist laughing for the baffled stare of said player <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T03:54:28-07:00","id":671798,"title":"","content":"Currently the culmination of around fifteen years of oWoD chronicles I've been playing in under my current GM, has an Earthbound, an Outsider and a Malfean, rising up to each rule/destroy/eat the world in their own way, with the PC's struggling to stop them.<br /> <br /> Imagination is key.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4572-vorcen","name":"Vorcen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T00:45:51-07:00","id":672975,"title":"","content":"Sounds like they break the old adage of &quot;You can not act on out of character information&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T11:49:30-07:00","id":673322,"title":"","content":"As I said in the other thread: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/671583-sorcerers-do-you-use-those-guys-in-your-games-and-if-you-do-how?p=671724#post671724\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...724#post671724</a><br /> <br /> I like to make my NPS`s in a way, that it is unclear, what exactly they are. Many signature powers can be re-created using different kinds of magic, and more often than not my more experienced players are contemplating 3 or more different kind of foes their opponent could possibly be.<br /> This can be done with almost all of the main splats, that are around in a usual game, and goes double for the more &quot;out-there&quot; sort of enemys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6112-seki","name":"Seki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T14:39:38-07:00","id":673441,"title":"","content":"I use TV or movie type villains and monsters and replace them with WoD splats. I've immediately freaked out a group of long playing RPers that are Garou and all of a sudden the Vamps they've tracked all of a sudden start flying like classic vamps and start lifting people up into the pitch night sky.<br /> <br /> or re-imagined vamps on my own ideas and say there are 5 ways to kill a Vamp once and for all...and theres no way of telling which way a vamp has to be killed. Only decapitation, fire, stake to the heart, holy water, sunlight can work. But only one will finally end them. <br /> <br /> Ghosts, spirits, monsters and myths I literally thriw the books out and base it on some other media or folklore.<br /> <br /> That generally freaks my guys out when the expected WoD rules bend away but acceptable horror monster rules come into play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T15:47:53-07:00","id":674654,"title":"","content":"You could probably justify it as the Vampires having the Flight Discipline, like Gargoyles do. Say that they don't need wings, and you don't even need to push things that far from established material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}